hadiths[77]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1721","On the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: Umar addressed the people at Al-Jabiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood in a position like this one of mine and said: ""Be good to my companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then there will come a people who will swear oaths before being asked to swear, and will give testimony before being asked to testify. Whoever among you wishes to attain the vastness of Paradise, let him hold fast to the congregation, for Satan is with the solitary one, and he is farther from two. And let no man be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. And whoever among you is pleased by his good deed and saddened by his evil deed, then he is a believer."""""
"1722","On the authority of Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather (Abdullah ibn Amr), who said: I witnessed Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) when the delegation of Hawazin came to him. They said: ""O Muhammad! We are a people and a clan, so bestow favor upon us, may Allah bestow favor upon you. For there has befallen us a calamity that is not hidden from you."" He said: ""Choose between your women, your wealth, and your children."" They said: ""You have given us the choice between our honor and our wealth; we choose our children."" He said: ""As for what belongs to me and to the Banu Abdul Muttalib, it is yours. So when I pray the Zuhr prayer, say: 'We seek intercession through Allah's Messenger with the believers, and through the believers with Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) regarding our women and our children.'"" So they did that. Then Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) said: ""As for what belongs to me and to the Banu Abdul Muttalib, it is yours."" The Muhajirun said: ""What belongs to us is for Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him)."" The Ansar said the same. Uyayna ibn Badr said: ""As for what belongs to me and to the Banu Fazara, no."" Al-Aqra' ibn Habis said: ""As for me and the Banu Tamim, no."" Abbas ibn Mirdas said: ""As for me and the Banu Sulaym, no."" The two tribes said: ""You lie; rather it is for Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him)."" Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) said: ""O people, return to them their women and their children. Whoever holds onto anything from the booty (fay'), for him there are six camels from the first thing Allah grants us as booty."" Then he mounted his riding camel, and the people clung to him, saying: ""Distribute our booty among us,"" until they forced him against a samura tree, and his cloak was snatched away. He said: ""O people, return my cloak to me. By Allah, if you had camels equal in number to the trees of Tihama, I would have distributed them among you. Then you would not find me miserly, nor cowardly, nor a liar."" Then he drew near to his camel, took a hair from its hump, placed it between his forefinger and middle finger, raised it, and said: ""O people, I have nothing from this booty, nor this hair, except the fifth (khums), and the fifth is returned to you. So return the needle and the thread. For stealing from the booty (ghulul) will be a source of shame, fire, and disgrace for its people on the Day of Resurrection."""""
"1723","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1723 Arabic Hadees: 2060"
"1724","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1724 Arabic Hadees: 2775"
"1725","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1725 Arabic Hadees: 2027"
"1726","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1726 Arabic Hadees: 1425"
"1727","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1727 Arabic Hadees: 2839"
"1728","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among us delivering a sermon, and part of his sermon was that he said: ""Behold, I am about to be summoned and I shall respond, and there will succeed me governors who will speak what they know and act according to what they recognize, and obedience to them is obedience. You will remain thus for a time. Then there will succeed you governors after them who will speak what they do not know and act according to what they do not recognize. Whoever advises them, assists them, and supports them, those have perished and caused others to perish. Associate with them bodily, but oppose them with your deeds, and bear witness that the good-doer is a good-doer, and the evil-doer is an evil-doer."""""
"1729","Abdur-Rahman ibn Shimasah said: I came to Aisha to ask her about something. She said: ""Where are you from?"" I said: ""A man from the people of Egypt."" She said: ""How was your governor for you in this expedition of yours?"" He said: ""We did not find any fault with him. If a man's camel died, he would give him a camel; if his slave died, he would give him a slave; and if he needed provisions, he would give him provisions."" She said: ""Nevertheless, what he did to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, my brother, will not prevent me from telling you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying in this house of mine: 'O Allah, whoever takes charge of any affair of my Ummah and makes it difficult for them, make it difficult for him; and whoever takes charge of any affair of my Ummah and is gentle with them, be gentle with him.'"""""
"1730","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1730 Arabic Hadees: 1089"
"1731","Abu Hurayrah reported: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to Abu al-Haytham: ""Do you have a servant?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Then when a captive comes to us, come to us."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) was brought two captives, without a third with them. Abu al-Haytham came to him, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Choose one of them."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, choose for me."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The consultant is trusted. Take this one, for I saw him praying, and treat him well."" His wife said: ""You will not fulfill what the Prophet (peace be upon him) said about him unless you free him."" He said: ""He is free."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah did not send a prophet nor a caliph except that he has two advisors: an advisor who commands him to good and forbids him from evil, and an advisor who does not spare him corruption. And whoever is protected from the evil advisor has been protected."""""
"1732","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1732 Arabic Hadees: 757"
"1733","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1733 Arabic Hadees: 747"
"1734","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1734 Arabic Hadees: 1384"
"1735","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1735 Arabic Hadees: 2197"
"1736","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1736 Arabic Hadees: 2493"
"1737","Al-Zuhri said: Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im used to narrate that it reached Mu'awiyah, while they were with him in a delegation from Quraysh, that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As was narrating that there would be a king from Qahtan. So he became angry, stood up, praised Allah as He deserves, then said: ""As for what follows: It has reached me that some men among you narrate hadiths that are not in the Book of Allah nor are they reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family). Those are your ignorant ones. So beware of the wishful thinking that misleads its people. Verily, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) say: 'This matter (authority) is in Quraysh; none opposes them except Allah throws him on his face, as long as they establish the religion.'"""""
"1738","Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdī Karib al-Kindī reported: He sat with ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, Abū al-Dardāʾ, and al-Ḥārith ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Kindī, and they recalled the ḥadīth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abū al-Dardāʾ said to ʿUbādah: ""O ʿUbādah, the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of such-and-such concerning the matter of the fifths (khumus)."" ʿUbādah said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer during their expedition beside a camel from the division (al-maqsim). When he gave the taslīm, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, took a single hair between his two fingertips, and said: 'This belongs to your spoils of war, and I have no share in it except my share alongside you, except the fifth—and the fifth is returned to you. So bring forth the thread and the needle, and what is greater than that and what is smaller. And do not commit ghulūl (embezzlement of spoils), for ghulūl is Fire and disgrace upon its perpetrators in this world and the Hereafter. And strive against people in the cause of Allah—Blessed and Exalted—near and far, and fear not in Allah the reproach of any reproacher. And uphold the limits of Allah in residence and travel. And strive in the way of Allah, for jihād is a gate from the gates of Paradise, tremendous, by which Allah—Blessed and Exalted—delivers from grief and anxiety.'"""""
"1739","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1739 Arabic Hadees: 2505"
"1740","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1740 Arabic Hadees: 1364"
"1741","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1741 Arabic Hadees: 1902"
"1742","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1742 Arabic Hadees: 2600"
"1743","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1743 Arabic Hadees: 1312"
"1744","Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated: I heard my father Buraydah say: We besieged Khaybar, and Abu Bakr took the banner but it was not conquered for him. Then Umar took it the next day and returned without it being conquered for him. The people suffered severe hardship and difficulty that day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I will give my banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; he will not return until it is conquered for him."" We spent the night with our souls at ease, knowing that the conquest would be tomorrow. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then stood up and called for the banner while the people were in their ranks. There was none of us who had a position with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he hoped to be the bearer of the banner. He called for Ali ibn Abi Talib, who was suffering from an eye ailment. He spat in his eyes and wiped them, then gave him the banner, and Allah granted conquest through him. And I was among those who stretched their necks toward it."
"1745","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) among nearly eighty men from Quraysh, none of whom was other than a Qurashi—by Allah, I never saw the visages of men more handsome than their faces on that day—they mentioned women and spoke about them, and he spoke with them until I wished he would fall silent. He said: Then he came to me, recited the tashahhud, then said: ""As for what follows: O people of Quraysh! You are the people of this matter as long as you do not disobey Allah; but if you disobey Him, He will send against you one who will contend with you as this rod contends with another rod in his hand."" Then he struck his rod, and behold, it was white, shining."
"1746","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1746 Arabic Hadees: 1632"
"1747","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1747 Arabic Hadees: 3511"
"1748","Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah reported that Aisha said: When the Prophet ﷺ became seriously ill and his pain intensified, he asked permission from his wives to be nursed in my house, and they granted him permission. The Prophet ﷺ came out between two men, his feet dragging on the ground, between Abbas and another man. Ubaydullah said: I informed Ibn Abbas about this, and he said: ""Do you know who the other man was?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""It was Ali.""Aisha used to narrate that the Prophet ﷺ said—after he entered his house and his pain intensified: ""Pour upon me from seven water skins that have not had their cords untied, so that I may give counsel to the people."" He was seated in a tub belonging to Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. Then we began pouring that water on him until he gestured to us that: ""You have done enough."" Then he went out to the people."
"1749","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1749 Arabic Hadees: 1952"
"1750","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1750 Arabic Hadees: 3031"
"1751","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1751 Arabic Hadees: 1069"
"1752","Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained in Mecca for ten years, following people in their dwellings during the seasons of ʿUkāẓ, Majanna, and the gatherings at Minā, saying: ""Who will give me shelter? Who will support me until I convey the message of my Lord, and for him is Paradise?"" Until a man would come from Yemen or from Muḍar — so he said — and his people would come to him and say: ""Beware of the youth of Quraysh, lest he seduce you."" And he would walk among their camps while they pointed at him with their fingers. Until Allah sent us to him from Yathrib; we gave him shelter and believed in him. Then a man from among us would go out, believe in him, and learn the Qurʾān from him, then return to his people, and they would embrace Islam through his Islam. Until there remained no dwelling of the Anṣār except that it contained a group of Muslims openly practicing Islam. Then they consulted together and said: ""Until when shall we leave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be driven out in the mountains of Mecca and live in fear?"" So seventy men from among us set out for him until they reached him during the season. We appointed to meet him at the mountain pass of al-ʿAqaba. We gathered there, man by man, two by two, until we had all assembled. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Shall we pledge allegiance to you?"" He said: ""You pledge allegiance to me upon hearing and obeying in energy and weariness, spending in hardship and ease, enjoining good and forbidding evil, and that you speak the truth for the sake of Allah, not fearing the blame of any critic. And that you support me and protect me when I come to you as you protect yourselves, your wives, and your children. And for you is Paradise."" He said: So we stood up and pledged allegiance to him. And al-Barāʾ ibn Maʿrūr — and he was among the youngest of them — took his hand and said: ""Gently, O people of Yathrib! For by Allah, we have not beaten the flanks of our camels except while knowing that he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And his expulsion today means separation from all the Arabs, the killing of your best, and that swords will bite you. So either you are a people who endure that, and your reward is with Allah, or you are a people who fear for yourselves cowardice; then make that clear, for it is an excuse for you before Allah."" They said: ""Remove your hand from us, O Saʿd! By Allah, we will never abandon this pledge, nor will we ever renounce it."" He said: So we stood up and pledged allegiance to him, and he took the pledge from us and stipulated the conditions, and promised us Paradise in return."
"1753","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1753 Arabic Hadees: 2497"
"1754","On the authority of An-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: We were sitting in the mosque, and Bashir was a man who restrained his speech. Then Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came and said: ""O Bashir ibn Sa'd! Do you preserve the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) regarding the rulers?"" Hudhayfah said: ""I preserve his sermon."" So Abu Tha'labah sat down. Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Prophethood will remain among you for as long as Allah wills it to remain, then Allah will raise it up when He wills to raise it up. Then there will be a Caliphate upon the methodology of Prophethood, so it will remain for as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will raise it up when He wills to raise it up. Then there will be a biting kingship, so it will remain for as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will raise it up when He wills to raise it up. Then there will be a coercive kingship, so it will remain for as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will raise it up when He wills to raise it up. Then there will be a Caliphate upon the methodology of Prophethood."" Then he fell silent."
"1755","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1755 Arabic Hadees: 18"
"1756","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1756 Arabic Hadees: 1023"
