"1758","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1758 Arabic Hadees: 1176"
"1759","On the authority of Abū Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) set out for Khaybar when he appointed Sibaʿ ibn ʿUrfuṭah over Medina. Abū Hurayrah said: I arrived in Medina as an emigrant and prayed the dawn prayer behind Sibaʿ. He recited in the first rakʿah: ""Kāf Hā Yā ʿAyn Ṣād"" (Maryam: 1), and in the second rakʿah: ""Woe to the defrauders"" (Al-Muṭaffifīn: 1). Abū Hurayrah said: So I said to myself during the prayer: ""Woe to the father of so-and-so! He has two measures: when he receives by measure, he takes in full, but when he gives by measure, he gives short."" When we finished our prayer, we went to Sibaʿ and he provisioned us with something until we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who had conquered Khaybar. He addressed the Muslims, so they gave us a share in their portions."
"1760","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1760 Arabic Hadees: 2059"
"1761","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1761 Arabic Hadees: 427"
