"1768","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1768 Arabic Hadees: 3355"
"1769","On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about good, but I used to ask him about evil out of fear that it might reach me. So I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we were in ignorance and evil, then Allah brought us this good (and we are in it), (and He brought you). Will there be any evil after this good (as there was before it)?"" He said: ""O Hudhayfah! Learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it,"" (three times). I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will there be good after this evil?"" He said: ""Yes."" (I said: ""What is the protection from it?"" He said: ""The sword."") I said: ""And will there be evil after that good?"" (And in a narration: ""I said: 'And will there be any remnant after the sword?'"") He said: ""Yes, and in it (and in a narration: 'There will be an emirate (and in a wording: a group) upon... and a truce upon') smoke (dakhan)."" I said: ""And what is its dakhan?"" He said: ""A people (and in another narration: 'There will be after me Imams (who follow other than my Sunnah, and) guide with other than my guidance; you will recognize from them and deny (and there will arise among them men whose hearts are the hearts of devils, in human bodies).')"" (And in another: ""The truce upon dakhan, what is it?"" He said: ""The hearts of a people will not return to what they were upon."") I said: ""Then will there be evil after that good?"" He said: ""Yes, (a blind and deaf fitnah, upon it) are callers at the gates of Hell; whoever answers them to it, they will throw him into it."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Describe them to us."" He said: ""They are from our skin (i.e., our people) and speak with our tongues."" I said: ""(O Messenger of Allah) Then what do you command me if I reach that?"" He said: ""Adhere to the Jama'ah ("
"1770","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1770 Arabic Hadees: 195"
"1771","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1771 Arabic Hadees: 2260"
"1772","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1772 Arabic Hadees: 2296"
"1773","On the authority of Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: We were encamped with Mu'awiyah after the killing of 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). Ka'b ibn Murrah al-Bahzi stood up and said: ""Were it not for something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I would not have stood in this position."" When Mu'awiyah heard the mention of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he made the people sit down and said: ""While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by, walking with a staff. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'A fitnah will surely emerge from beneath the feet of this one — or from between his legs —' meaning 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). 'This one on that day, and whoever follows him, will be upon guidance.'""Ibn Hawalah al-Azdi stood up from near the pulpit and said: ""Are you the one who witnessed this?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""By Allah, I was present at that gathering, and had I known that there was someone in the army who would corroborate me, I would have been the first to speak of it."""""
