"1785","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1785 Arabic Hadees: 3415"
"1786","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1786 Arabic Hadees: 727"
"1787","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1787 Arabic Hadees: 1167"
"1788","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, you are dearer to me than myself, and you are dearer to me than my family, and dearer to me than my children. And when I am in my house, I remember you and I cannot bear it until I come to you and look at you. And when I remember my death and your death, I know that when you enter Paradise, you will be raised with the prophets, and I fear that when I enter Paradise, I will not see you."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reply to him until Jibreel came down with this verse: ""And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger - those will be with the ones upon whom Allah has bestowed favor of the prophets, the steadfast affirmers of truth, the martyrs and the righteous. And excellent are those as companions."" (An-Nisa: 69)"
"1789","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1789 Arabic Hadees: 674"
"1790","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1790 Arabic Hadees: 2394"
"1791","On the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, who said: Ziyad wanted to appoint Imran ibn Husayn as governor over Khurasan, but he refused. His companions said to him: ""Did you leave Khurasan so that you could be its governor?"" He said: ""By Allah, it would not please me that I should pray in its heat while you pray in its coolness. And I fear that if I were in the thick of battle against the enemy, a letter from Ziyad would come to me; if I proceeded, I would perish, and if I returned, my neck would be struck."" Then he wanted to appoint al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari over it, and he complied with his command. Imran said: ""Is there no one to call al-Hakam for me?"" The messenger went, and al-Hakam came to him and entered. Imran said to al-Hakam: ""Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah, Blessed and Exalted'?"" He said: ""Yes."" Imran said: ""Praise be to Allah,"" or ""Allah is Greatest."""""
"1792","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1792 Arabic Hadees: 673"
"1793","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1793 Arabic Hadees: 678"
"1794","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1794 Arabic Hadees: 2424"
"1795","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1795 Arabic Hadees: 677"
"1796","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1796 Arabic Hadees: 839"
"1797","On the authority of Abu Nadrah, who said: We were with Jabir ibn Abdullah when he said: ""The people of Iraq will soon have no qafiz nor dirham brought to them."" We asked: ""From where will that be?"" He said: ""From the direction of the non-Arabs, who will prevent that."" Then he said: ""The people of Syria will soon have no dinar nor mudd brought to them."" We asked: ""From where will that be?"" He said: ""From the direction of the Romans, who will prevent that."" He said: Then he paused for a moment, then said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'There will be at the end of my Ummah a Caliph who will scatter wealth profusely, not counting it.'"" He said: I said to Abu Nadrah and Abu Al-Ala: ""Do you two think that it is Umar ibn Abdul Aziz?"" They both said: ""No."""""
